nodecode-aurora is a rewrite of Ntizar's Ntizar/hermes-aurora:

https://github.com/Ntizar/hermes-aurora
commit dcf5b271e76bb541e7822b029b6de08fa2244582

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 David Antizar (Ntizar) (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's two tools are tools of the same names here,
aurora_search and aurora_validate, and the same calls as Lisp verbs,
aurora:lookup and aurora:check. The census the Python shipped in
data/censo.json is shipped unchanged and read with the image's own JSON reader,
and the lookup scores a query the way the original did -- the same namespaced
name, class and filing-text weights with the same base-class bonus, the same
Spanish-to-census synonym table, the same stopwords, the same accent folding,
the same sort by score then shorter name, the same caps of 20 families and 25
classes, and the same fields out of each family: pack, demo, classes, title,
what not to use and the catalogue markup. The validator keeps every check and
every verdict: unknown classes, packs used but not linked (all.css satisfying
all of them), gradient, backdrop-filter and !important outside the crystal
layer and the hiding helpers, hand-written colours, emoji outside the
attribution, the exact footer, a second h1, and the four warnings. Nothing was
added that reaches a service: the plugin's four skills are here as the manual
topic (help :aurora), which is one prose text a request can read, plus one /aurora
command.

What was left out: the skills as four separate skill files. Their doctrine is
condensed into the one manual topic, and the fourth -- the openui-lang prompt
for letting a model compose the design system's own component language at
runtime -- is not carried at all, since this cell answers the markup that
exists rather than generating a component spec. The JSON envelopes both tools
answered are now the lines a model reads, and the section adds the four knobs
the original had none of (limit, channel, footer, require_footer); a failure
the Python wrote as an "error" member is here an ERROR: line, and a folder
whose census file is gone refuses its start instead of answering nothing.
